==English==

===Etymology===
As if {{m|en|smack|smacked|hit}} in the {{m|en|gob||mouth (Irish / Scottish gaelic)}}.

Attested since 1959, from Northern English dialect, particularly Liverpool, popularized via television.<ref>[http://www.worldwidewords.org/qa/qa-gob1.htm World Wide Words: Gobsmacked]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɒb.smækt/}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 gobsmacked.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

